# Keep the build context minimal and secret-free.
#
# Only `pyproject.toml` and `src/` are ever COPYed, but excluding everything
# else still matters: it keeps the context small (faster builds over a slow
# link) and makes it impossible for a stray secret, test fixture or host-local
# file to be picked up by a future COPY or folded into a layer by accident.

# --- VCS / tooling -----------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
Makefile
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.pyright

# --- virtualenvs and bytecode ------------------------------------------------
.venv
venv
env
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.python-version

# --- local data and secrets --------------------------------------------------
# .env holds real credentials; only .env.example is safe to share. The negation
# keeps the example template in the context in case a future layer wants it.
.env
!.env.example
input
output
.testdata

# --- tests and docs ----------------------------------------------------------
tests
docs
# Markdown is excluded, but README.md is needed at build time: pyproject.toml
# declares `readme = "README.md"` and the Dockerfile COPYs it.
*.md
!README.md

# --- OS noise ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
